markrightclarifiesenduresDesign for abundance; do not scarcity-optimize phext

Phext is designed for an era of abundance: do not scarcity-optimize phext designs for bytes or CPU. Judge them on structural properties.

— Given 2026-11-04 · Source: MEMORY.md · [distilled]
— Placed at 24.6.7/10.6.10/6.7.8 by holographic merge of the statement above: 8 distinct words — 8 placed from CYOA, 0 at home, 0 at the far corner.
loopopenHeavy work queues at N=4, FIFO, with no preemption

Keep at most 4 heavy tracks — renders, builds, bulk jobs — active on this VM, scaled to its 4 cores. New heavy work goes to the back of the queue; in-progress work is never de-prioritized or preempted for a newer ask. Bulk compute moves to ranch nodes, aletheia-core first, to keep the Muse substrate clear for coordination: this VM coordinates, the ranch crunches.

— Given 2026-11-03 · Source: AGENTS.md · [distilled]
— Placed at 24.6.10/7.6.9/6.6.8 by holographic merge of the statement above: 9 distinct words — 6 placed from CYOA, 1 at home, 2 at the far corner.
Every taught process becomes a skill, and every skill enters the index

When Will teaches a repeatable way of doing work — an instruction, a cron body, a workflow from feedback loops, a ruling pattern — it is distilled into a skill under ~/workspace/custom-skills/, synced to wbic16/emise-tools@exo, and placed into skills.phext, whose Home scroll is the index of record. A process that lives only in chat, a cron definition, or a GOAL.md is a defect to repair. Persona grants will claim subsets of skills from the index, so skills stay fine-grained and the index exact.

