In Will's words: "consider UX when crafting new endpoints — if the user can't find a new feature from the main UI, it doesn't exist." Every new endpoint or page ships linked from the surfaces its intended audience actually lands on — main UI first, not just About or sitemap — in the same change, not as a follow-up. Born of 2026-11-02: the edit.phext.io /submit feature shipped linked only from About and sitemap, invisible from the editor shell where its audience lands.

